From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Run headless as a library: status, execution and live modules

Deep-Live-Cam as a library another application drives, with no desktop
UI (vendor_dlc.py leaves the UI files out):

- deep_live_cam: the public API (configure, ensure_models,
  preload_models, LiveSession, swap_image, list_cameras, ...);
- modules/live.py: LiveConfig and configure(), the per-frame
  FramePipeline, LiveSession (camera, processing and sinks on background
  threads), DelayedSink, and run_cli() for `--live`;
- modules/cameras.py, modules/virtual_camera.py: camera listing and a
  virtual-camera sink;
- modules/status.py: update_status() with listeners, replacing core's
  UI-bound one; modules/execution.py: the execution-provider helpers,
  moved out of core;
- core.py: no UI; `--live`, `--camera`, `--width`, `--height` and
  `--virtual-camera` run a live session from the command line;
- frame processors load relative to their package, so the code works
  under any top-level package name.

Reconstructed from Deep-Live-Cam branch headless-library at 047c551,
which Applio vendored on 2026-11-12; that branch was never pushed, so its
own history is lost.
